name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T04:57:45-08:00","id":1434368,"title":"","content":"I preordered the game last month on my birthday. I'm ready for tomorrow...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T06:43:44-08:00","id":1434378,"title":"","content":"Optimistic. I'm not a gamer or a video game player but I bought this one. I saw some sneak peak and gameplay from who already played the game. The only important thing for me is the fact that the game seems to capture the right vibe of werewolf the apocalypse. The character is very charismatic and the whole pack seems cool.<br /> I will love the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T06:55:56-08:00","id":1434379,"title":"","content":"I've preordered the game as soon as it was possible on epicgames. I'm waiting for it too long so I'm, excited. Even when it would be a crap I am happy taht it's WtA and I will play it anyway with smile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T07:07:09-08:00","id":1434380,"title":"","content":"I preordered, too.<br /> <br /> But, &quot;Heart of the Forest&quot; is the first game that was actually released - although it is a different type of game.<br /> <br /> And, I once heard about &quot;Warrior of the Apocalypse&quot;, a werewolf protagonist jump-n-run for SEGA consoles. But no idea if it really was released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T14:28:54-08:00","id":1434530,"title":"","content":"I'd describe it as decent. Fun but not likely to bring in new fans, not like Bloodlines did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T17:25:13-08:00","id":1434544,"title":"","content":"I saw a playthrough the beginning and I have to say the voice acting for the main hero and villain suck. Our villian sounds like a teenager girl which ruins any scene where she is cool and badass. Our hero can\u2019t emote for shit. When he\u2019s suppose to be consumed rage over the death of his wife he just sounds barely annoyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1685-looker","name":"Looker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T23:27:02-08:00","id":1434558,"title":"","content":"I am enjoying the game. Combat is fun. Crinos is fast strong and deadly as it should be. I like lupus form and the way it sneak past the guards. Is the game worth buying? For hardcore toxic fanboy like me yes. I don't look at the game searching for flaws. I go with the flow enjoying it cause I was waiting for WtA game since 90's and that's far too long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T00:48:58-08:00","id":1434564,"title":"","content":"My brother called me up on the phone earlier today and spent like 15 minutes telling me how bad the game was and how salty he was that he'd spent $40 on it. He said it looked and played like an old early PS2 era game complete with tank controls. The voice acting and sound in general were pretty bad. He said he didn't enjoy the gameplay at all, just going into mostly empty rooms and fighting waves of enemies using bad controls. He said he played for about 30 minutes and then that was it, he was done with it. Hope other people have more fun than he did.<br /> <br /> I might grab it someday but I'll definitely be waiting for a big sale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T01:22:45-08:00","id":1434565,"title":"","content":"As a Long time Fan of Werewolf the Apocalypse setting and now Earthblood as well, <br /> <br /> First off I remember the First Werewolf the Apocalyspe Video Game failure comes to mind the one that shortly partialy made after Bloodlines came out it was going to like Bloodlines like for Werewolf that main character was a White Howler he had the chance of ether stay a true Garou of fall to the Wyrm. <br /> <br /> Now onto EarthBlood yes it's action with some RPG touches, I've played the Assassian's Creed series I'm familar with the edges like powers and build up system, side missions are ok <br /> <br /> Good Eye Candy such as the Whskey signs from King, The soda machines on the First area I'm atill trying to figure what part of Pentex company there from. Endron Doesn't have a Presdent it has Them or They,<br /> <br /> LW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3380-martian1912","name":"Martian1912","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T01:44:42-08:00","id":1434569,"title":"","content":"While I was on the fence about it and nothing's really urging me to plop down new game price money on this... I'm getting a weird feeling that Earthblood is getting graded on one hell of a curve by the big reviewers. CP '77 and Hades seem like they've done more good for Earthblood than anything in Earthblood simply by burning reviewers on AAA games that might not even be playable at launch, while lower budget games redoing old standard game-styles with some new character to them feel like a breath of fresh air simply by doing what they're supposed to do on release.<br /> <br /> Though it really sounds like Earthblood could have leaned harder into being a bit retro since everyone seems to point out how dated it feels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T07:17:14-08:00","id":1434596,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Only about 3 hours in, but I'm loving it so far. Enjoying the various Pentex references throughout and the main character and supporting cast are fine. Definitely could've used some better voice acting. It's been giving me Terminator: Resistance feelings, which was reviewed poorly, but I found it to be an excellent game, no doubt helped in part due to my love of the source material. Similar instance here, I'd say. Could Earthblood use some more polish? Absolutely. Developers could have certainly used a bigger budget(couldn't we all) and it's definitely not a AAA game, but it shouldn't stop any World of Darkness fan from having a ton of fun with it.<br /> <br /> I'm satisfied. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T07:42:23-08:00","id":1434599,"title":"","content":"Okay, so from an artist's/Lore fan's perspective;<br /> <br /> The visuals are great, the crinos forms LOOK crinos and behave crinos. You can move freely in lupus and lupus animation is solid. You can tell when a character is a Silver Fang or a Red Talon. The Caern Totem and other spirits look fitting.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">But then there is this Red Talon Caern that apparently does not tend to their spirits at all. Led by an Uktena(??) and they are framing her and her sept as WRONG for not liking humans.<br /> <br /> You also mostly fight humans/fomori, which works just fine but you see the same models most of the game. There is also the issue of having a Fianna Ahroun do stealth, which works as well as it does in canon. Lots of crinos use. Given Cahal is in a pack, too, it is just weird how much he does alone.<br /> <br /> Thrall of the Wyrm seems to be something of an endgame, since the Silver Fang leader gets killed by Cahal once he succumbs.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For what it is, it is not bad. Just disjointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 02-05-2021, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T07:54:30-08:00","id":1434600,"title":"","content":"So fat I'm still enjoying game making side quests and looking around for any new things to read. Fomori are quite tough and I smiled as they appeared.<br /> <br /> I know that I'll try to play on hard and in stealth only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T09:08:35-08:00","id":1434610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1433329-thoughts-on-earthblood?p=1434599#post1434599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so from an artist's/Lore fan's perspective;<br /> <br /> The visuals are great, the crinos forms LOOK crinos and behave crinos. You can move freely in lupus and lupus animation is solid. You can tell when a character is a Silver Fang or a Red Talon. The Caern Totem and other spirits look fitting.<br /> <br /> But then there is this Red Talon Caern that apparently does not tend to their spirits at all. Led by an Uktena(??) and they are framing her and her sept as WRONG for not liking humans.<br /> <br /> You also mostly fight humans/fomori, which works just fine but you see the same models most of the game. There is also the issue of having a Fianna Ahroun do stealth, which works as well as it does in canon. Lots of crinos use. Given Cahal is in a pack, too, it is just weird how much he does alone.<br /> <br /> Thrall of the Wyrm seems to be something of an endgame, since the Silver Fang leader gets killed by Cahal once he succumbs.<br /> <br /> For what it is, it is not bad. Just disjointed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Should probably hide the spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T10:13:15-08:00","id":1434621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1433329-thoughts-on-earthblood?p=1434610#post1434610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Should probably hide the spoilers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for reminding me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T11:11:48-08:00","id":1434628,"title":"","content":"But is it good enough to justify putting epic store on my computer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1069-archmage-joda","name":"Archmage Joda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T12:58:29-08:00","id":1434636,"title":"","content":"I've read a few reviews now, and they say the game is repetitive? All stealth till stealth breaks, then full destruction crinos, over and over again? Made the game sound really basic and PS2 level. Are you guys finding more richness to it? Content that could inspire a TT game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T13:30:34-08:00","id":1434640,"title":"","content":"There is at least one scene that is worth everything but it's cause it's involving my favourite tribe. Game is fast to play and fast to finish and that's the sad part. I think ending is very good , pure WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T16:24:25-08:00","id":1434647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pwtucker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1433329-thoughts-on-earthblood?p=1434636#post1434636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read a few reviews now, and they say the game is repetitive? All stealth till stealth breaks, then full destruction crinos, over and over again? Made the game sound really basic and PS2 level. Are you guys finding more richness to it? Content that could inspire a TT game?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thats pretty much what it seems from the few AP videos I've seen. Apparently others here are enjoying it but from the vids I've seen it just looks really dated, basic and repetitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T01:26:04-08:00","id":1434671,"title":"","content":"So far it's been pretty simple but fun. If you are looking for &quot;Witcher-like&quot; conversation paths and depth of story this isn't going to be for you. It's a linear action game story and I'm fine with that. So far yes it has been stealth until you either insta lose from being detected by security cameras and the game ends, or you get to go Crinos and kill everything. They got the Crinos form right, I've been having fun with it and I only have it partially built up. Graphics could be better, I'm playing it on an Xbox Series X and this definitely looks like an older Xbox One game. That's my opinion so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T07:02:41-08:00","id":1434685,"title":"","content":"I almost finished the game and it's really dark, mature, and it hits the right targets. I hope the 5th edition will have a lot of this kind of mature and dark vibes and less urban-fantasy stuff.<br /> The depiction of the tribe is absolutely nice and the developers truly knew what they were doing.<br /> The game touches many things about wta in a very deep way, rage at the top of them. Nice work.<br /> Btw, I'm not a gamer. I know nothing about graphics and so on. I'm talking about the story and the vibe.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I totally support this kind of tribal-political fact about the Uktena elder leading the talons. We should break some political stereotype of werewolf. It is clear from the story that the garou are very few, so few that some of them break the litany to cooperate with humans. </div></div> </div> </div></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 02-06-2021, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T08:21:47-08:00","id":1434687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1433329-thoughts-on-earthblood?p=1434685#post1434685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I totally support this kind of tribal-political fact about the Uktena elder leading the talons. We should break some political stereotype of werewolf. It is clear from the story that the garou are very few, so few that some of them break the litany to cooperate with humans. </div></div> </div> </div></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The issue is that it doesn't break the Litany to work with humans, in fact Uktena are one of the tribes who have dedicated ties to humanity of all kinds. MOST tribes work with humans, because kinfolk ARE human. Red Talons are an outlier as a tribe in many MANY aspects.<br /> <br /> The whole 'working with humans is rare and BAD' is more of a forced take on the garou caring for stuff BEYOND humans. And while the game did in fact handle it better than I expected, it still is something that is not part of the game before W5. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T08:52:58-08:00","id":1434689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1433329-thoughts-on-earthblood?p=1434687#post1434687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The issue is that it doesn't break the Litany to work with humans, in fact Uktena are one of the tribes who have dedicated ties to humanity of all kinds. MOST tribes work with humans, because kinfolk ARE human. Red Talons are an outlier as a tribe in many MANY aspects.<br /> <br /> The whole 'working with humans is rare and BAD' is more of a forced take on the garou caring for stuff BEYOND humans. And while the game did in fact handle it better than I expected, it still is something that is not part of the game before W5. </div></div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Of course, is a new thing, and I really like it. Actually in the game is a litany breach. Talking with one of the lambda mankind the guy clearly says 'I knwo what you are''. Those are not all kinfolk. Also, Rodko himslef at the start of the game doesn't want to work with humans. They are clearly talking about normal humans, not kinfolk. The red talons pack is savage in the game, as we all espect. I find it really cool to see an Uktena primitive member guiding them.</div></div> </div> </div></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T18:14:47-08:00","id":1434720,"title":"","content":"I just played the intro as of now.<br /> <br /> I think it is okay as a video game, but I don't like that they (so far) are off in some aspekts of the game compared with the Setting.<br /> <br /> Also they narrate that Gaia came from the Triat, and I like it to be uncertain, which was first...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_li